{
    "background_story": "Jream was a struggling playwright in 1920s New York City, working multiple jobs to make ends meet. One day, while sweeping the floors at the local theater, he met Oscar Hammerstein II, the renowned lyricist and librettist. Hammerstein, impressed by Jream's passion for storytelling, took him under his wing and became his mentor. Under Hammerstein's guidance, Jream's writing flourished, and he began to develop his own unique voice. Together, they collaborated on several projects, with Jream learning the intricacies of crafting compelling characters and storylines. As Jream's skills improved, he started to make a name for himself in the theater community, eventually earning a spot as a writer for a major Broadway production. Jream never forgot the lessons he learned from Hammerstein and continued to honor his mentor's legacy through his own work.",
